rows=[]
def row(domain,location,expectation,implementation,uncertainty=None):rows.append(dict(domain=domain,source_location=location,source_expectation=expectation,implementation=implementation,unresolved=uncertainty))
row('Indications and schedule','NCCP pp1,8','00216a–f includes breast and colorectal contexts. Reference dose: 1250 mg/m² BID, days 1–14, q21d. Adjuvant colon/TNBC: eight cycles. Advanced disease: until progression or intolerance. A 1000 mg/m² start may be considered for selected patients.','Existing stable indications and treatment phases are preserved. Exact context must be selected; no breast/CRC evidence transplant.','Indications d, e and f carry the source off-label consent/policy footnote. No new indication is inferred from a duration paragraph.')
row('Eligibility and baseline tests','NCCP pp1–2','ECOG 0–2; baseline FBC, renal and liver profile; DPD testing unless previously tested. FBC, renal and liver profile before each cycle. Disease monitoring follows the consultant plan.','ECOG review retained; monitoring is carried into patient/KB/support work. No universal imaging or tumour-marker interval is invented.')
row('DPD and exclusions','NCCP pp2,6; EMA pp7–9','Complete DPD deficiency excludes treatment. Partial deficiency needs an individualised reduced start and careful monitoring. Renal impairment can confound uracil phenotyping. Severe prior reaction, hypersensitivity, pregnancy/lactation and recent brivudine are exclusions.','Existing exclusion rules retained. Guidance adds the uracil caveat and genotype consideration, distinguishing initial partial-DPD titration from toxicity-dose re-escalation.','There is no universal partial-DPD percentage in this regimen; DPD status is not calculated from renal function.')
row('Baseline counts discrepancy','NCCP p3 prose; EMA p5 section4.2','NCCP advises caution for ANC <1.5 or platelets <100; EMA says these patients should not be treated.','Consultant review explicitly identifies both sources and states no automatic initiation. Boundary and missing-input cases retained.','This wording difference remains for clinical/pharmacy resolution. The subsequent-dose platelet threshold of 75 is not baseline clearance.')
row('Unscheduled within-cycle counts','NCCP p3','Interrupt for ANC <1 or platelets <75. ANC 1–<1.5 differs from the next-dose recovery threshold.','Distinct within-cycle hold/review rules retained. No recurrence percentage is automatically applied within a cycle.')
row('Haematology recurrence','NCCP p3 Table1','ANC 1–1.49 or platelets 50–74.9: 100/75/50/stop for events 1–4. ANC 0.5–0.99 or platelets 25–49.9: 75/50/stop/stop. ANC <0.5 or platelets <25: stop, with a first-event consultant exception to delay then 50%.','Both current recovery counts and both episode nadirs are required for numerical restart. A historical permanent-stop threshold remains valid before complete recovery.','Printed decimal bands are treated as continuous intervals below the upper threshold, not silently rounded. The severe first-event exception never produces an automatic 50% restart.')
row('Prior dose and non-escalation','NCCP p2; EMA p5','After a toxicity reduction, the dose must not be increased. Omitted toxicity doses are not replaced.','Previous prescribed percentage gates all 75/50% restart outputs. Unknown or lower history produces review. The 100% table row remains a review. Percentages use the documented original start and are not compounded.','Initial partial-DPD titration is a distinct consultant-managed exception.')
row('Renal thresholds and starting-dose discrepancy','NCCP p3 Table2; EMA p6 section4.2','NCCP: CrCl 30–50 gives 75% of original dose; 51–80 gives no adjustment; below 30 or dialysis is not recommended. EMA distinguishes 1250 and 1000 mg/m² starts and contraindicates severe renal impairment.','A documented 1250 start with a genuine baseline or safe prior-dose context gives 75%. Reduced, other or unknown starts/history require source reconciliation. Severe impairment and dialysis actions are retained with clearer attribution.','NCCP/EMA reduced-start disagreement and 50–51 mL/min decimal gap remain unresolved numerically. No silent rounding or dose escalation.')
row('Hepatic function and attribution','NCCP p3 Table2,p6 Table6; EMA pp7–8','NCCP specifies no routine hepatic adjustment. Treatment-related bilirubin >3 or ALT/AST >2.5 requires a hold. EMA lists severe hepatic impairment as a contraindication.','Baseline or assessed non-treatment-related elevations prompt review; current or uncertain-attribution elevations retain hold and clarification. Severe hepatic exclusion is separate.','Source recovery wording uses OR. The tool does not clear one affected test while another remains abnormal and never issues restart clearance from an isolated normal result.')
row('General and diarrhoea recurrence','NCCP pp4–5 Tables3–4','Grade 2 events 1/2/3/4: 100/75/50/stop. Grade 3 events 1/2/3: 75/50/stop. Grade 4: stop, with a first-event consultant exception.','Current hold, documented peak/recurrence/recovery and previous-dose checks. A grade 3 episode remains controlling after partial improvement to grade 2; terminal recurrence stops before full recovery.','Nocturnal stools appear in both low-grade and grade 2 NCCP rows. UI acknowledges the overlap; EMA patient stop-and-contact advice is preserved.')
row('HFS source-specific grading','NCCP p5 Table5; EMA p7','Grade 2/3 requires interruption until grade ≤1. Grade 3 requires a subsequent reduction, with no percentage specified.','Input descriptions now use NCCP table 5; hold and unquantified consultant-review pathways retained.','A 75% reduction is not imported from general table 3, which applies to toxicities not separately specified.')
row('Grade attribution','NCCP p4 Table3 and p5 Tables4–5','Table 3 cites CTCAE v4. Table 4 contains legacy bands; table 5 is regimen-specific.','Diarrhoea/HFS attributes identify their actual source table. Generic CTCAE v5 mucositis/other-toxicity UI aids are explicitly distinguished from source v4.','Generic displayed aids are not represented as regimen-specific source definitions; the clinician confirms the grade.')
row('Dehydration','EMA p7 section4.4','Grade 2 or higher dehydration requires immediate interruption. Restart only after rehydration and correction/control of the cause.','Active dehydration or an uncontrolled cause holds treatment. Even recovered/controlled status requires kidney, causative-toxicity, history and restart-plan review.')
row('Cardiac and severe skin safety','EMA pp8,10 section4.4; leaflet p44','Significant cardiac history requires caution. Chest pain prompts stop/contact. Severe skin reactions such as SJS/TEN require permanent discontinuation.','New optional cardiac-history review, current-chest-pain hold/urgent assessment and severe-skin stop. No automatic cardiac rechallenge.')
row('Interactions','EMA pp8,10 section4.4–4.5','Brivudine interval: at least four weeks. Coumarin: close INR/PT monitoring. Phenytoin: plasma-level monitoring.','Brivudine exclusion now cites the freshly retrieved EMA source. Optional monitoring prompts do not calculate interacting-drug doses.')
row('Limits of automation','NCCP/EMA clinical-judgement statements','Other clinical cautions, comorbidities and symptoms still require clinical review.','All inputs remain optional. Blank/null values are unassessed. A generic toxicity field does not replace clinical assessment or authorise prescribing.','This bounded protocol audit does not establish independent clinical approval, global consistency, device installation/printing, camera QR scanning or production deployment.')
write('source-criteria-matrix.json',rows)
